## Update (turn 3): early-time survival criterion — now drafted in sections/theory.tex
Closed form (phase I: p = p0 e^{-alpha lambda_P t}; capture when w crosses the p-nullcline
w^2 = lambda_P p/(s - p c)):  Phi_j = max_p [log eps_j + G_j(p) - 1/2 log(lambda_P p/(s_j - p c_j))],
G_j(p) = [s_j(p0-p) - c_j(p0^2-p^2)/2 - lambda log(p0/p)] / (alpha lambda_P). Survive iff Phi_j > 0 and s_j^2/c_j > 4 lambda.
Pilot vs integrating the 2-D ODE: 297/300 random settings (lambda_P = lambda, alpha = 1;
`notes/pilot/survival_criterion_equal_decay.*`); 371/400 with lambda_P/lambda in [0.3,3], alpha in [0.3,3]
(`survival_criterion_general.*`); failures concentrate at lambda_P > lambda and alpha > 1. Fixed-point bound alone: 183/300, 237/400.
Masking: Bernoulli context mask (keep prob q), target = complement, stationary x with spectrum S_k, variance sigma^2:
s_k = q(1-q)(S_k - sigma^2), c_k = q(q S_k + (1-q) sigma^2) -> only above-average-power Fourier directions can survive.
